// =====================================================================
// SCENE 4 · GAP 2: THE AUDITORIUM (00:00)
// Night Anin takes the rooftop key, slips Fal a note moving their study
// session to the auditorium, and "checks" the flagpole, actually
// loosening a screw at its base.
//
// NOTES FOR THE PROGRAMMER
// - Every "//" comment is a stage direction for you, not in-game text.
// - WRITING RULE: every line night Anin says is true. She withholds,
//   she never lies. Please don't add lines without checking with N.
// - Same gap rules as Scene 2: no NPCs, Kirana's bed empty, clocks
//   frozen at 00:00.
// - NO master key, stage light or ladder in this scene (no assets yet).
// - Commands used (new ones marked NEW):
//     <<gap_mode true/false>>         gap visuals on/off
//     <<quest_start "id" "Title">>    start / show a quest
//     <<quest_update "id" "Title">>   update the quest objective
//     <<scene_transition "Location">> fade + load a location
//     <<give_item "id">>              add item to inventory
//     <<remove_item "id">>            remove item from inventory
//     <<blur_action "id">>        NEW Anin kneels; her hands blur exactly
//                                     like <<blur_writing>> in Gap 1. Slow
//                                     metallic squeak, a screw turning.
//                                     The player must NOT see which way.
//     <<end_gap>>                     second hand moves, fade to Dec 10
// - ORDER (linear, no fail state):
//     rooftop key -> write note -> slide it into Fal's locker
//     -> auditorium -> flag -> flagpole base -> bed
//   Fal's locker shows only once $gap2_rooftop_key is true, and the
//   flagpole base only once $gap2_seen_flag is true (ActiveIfYarnVariable
//   with Follow Changes), so the order holds.
// - The ROOFTOP KEY stays in Anin's inventory at the end. Day 3 starts
//   with it in her blazer pocket.
// - World state for Day 3: the flag is still crooked, one screw at the
//   flagpole base is loose, and the auditorium note is in Fal's locker.
// =====================================================================


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// DORM — 00:00
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

title: Gap2_Start
tags: scene4 gap2 dorm
---
<<gap_mode true>>
// Lets the Dorm door run Gap2_Dorm_Door instead of leaving freely.
<<set $story_exit to true>>
<<set $gap2_rooftop_key to false>>
<<set $gap2_note_placed to false>>
<<set $gap2_seen_flag to false>>
<<set $gap2_pole_done to false>>

// Anin opens her eyes. Kirana's bed is empty again, the blanket flat.
// Double reading: first play = the notes failed to save him.
// Replay = the notes didn't break the loop.
Anin: The notes didn't work. Something else, then.
<<quest_start "gap2" "Keep him off the roof">>
// Interactables: Gap2_Dorm_Clock, Gap2_Dorm_KiranaBed, Gap2_Dorm_Door
===

title: Gap2_Dorm_Clock
tags: scene4 gap2 dorm interactable
---
Anin: Midnight. Still.
===

title: Gap2_Dorm_KiranaBed
tags: scene4 gap2 dorm interactable
---
Anin: Gone, like last time.
===

title: Gap2_Dorm_Door
tags: scene4 gap2 dorm interactable
---
<<if $gap2_pole_done is false>>
    Anin: Not the rooftop. Not tonight.
    <<scene_transition "LockerRoom">>
<<else>>
    <<jump Gap2_Dorm_End>>
<<endif>>
===


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// LOCKER ROOM — 00:00
// Interactables: Gap2_KeyHook, Gap2_FalLocker
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

title: Gap2_KeyHook
tags: scene4 gap2 lockers interactable
---
// Hook tag: ROOFTOP. Key is on the hook.
<<if $gap2_rooftop_key is false>>
    // Double reading: true both ways. He won't die on the roof,
    // because he'll die in the auditorium.
    Anin: He won't go up there tonight.
    <<give_item "rooftop_key">>
    <<set $gap2_rooftop_key to true>>
<<else>>
    Anin: Empty.
<<endif>>
===

title: Gap2_FalLocker
tags: scene4 gap2 lockers interactable
---
// Fal's locker, rocket sticker on the door. It stays LOCKED.
<<if $gap2_note_placed is true>>
    Anin: He'll find it.
<<else>>
    <<sfx "write_and_place_note">>
    Anin: He still meets me here after school. So we'll study somewhere else.
    // Writing animation. Unlike Gap 1, this note is READABLE and NOT
    // blurred. Show the line below in a handwritten-note style if you
    // can. It is harmless on its face, and unsigned.
    Anin: "Let's study in the auditorium today instead of the library. It's quieter. Same time."
    Anin: Somewhere quiet. Nobody goes there after school.
    // Anin slides the note through the vent slot of Fal's locker.
    // No key needed.
    <<set $gap2_note_placed to true>>
    <<quest_update "gap2" "Go to the auditorium">>
<<endif>>
===


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// AUDITORIUM — 00:00
// Dark and silent. The flag hangs still in the middle of the room.
// Interactables: Gap2_Hoop, Gap2_MicStand, Gap2_Flag, Gap2_FlagpoleBase
// Gap2_FlagpoleBase is only interactable after Gap2_Flag.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

title: Gap2_Auditorium_Enter
tags: scene4 gap2 auditorium
---
Anin: Tomorrow's ceremony is supposed to happen here.
===

title: Gap2_Hoop
tags: scene4 gap2 auditorium interactable
---
Anin: Nobody's played here since they started preparing for graduation.
===

title: Gap2_MicStand
tags: scene4 gap2 auditorium interactable
---
// On the stage. Scene 8's confrontation happens here.
Anin: The stage is ready. Just waiting for tomorrow.
===

title: Gap2_Flag
tags: scene4 gap2 auditorium interactable
---
<<if $gap2_pole_done is true>>
    Anin: It's done.
<<else>>
    <<sfx "flag_cloth">>
    Anin: It's crooked.
    // Double reading: first play = she knows Fal can't leave things
    // imperfect. Replay = this is the trigger she's setting up.
    Anin: He'll want to fix it.
    <<set $gap2_seen_flag to true>>
    // Enable Gap2_FlagpoleBase now.
<<endif>>
===

title: Gap2_FlagpoleBase
tags: scene4 gap2 auditorium interactable
---
<<if $gap2_seen_flag is false>>
    // Should not be reachable; base is disabled until the flag is examined.
<<elseif $gap2_pole_done is false>>
    Anin: Let me check the base.
    <<blur_action "flagpole_base">>
    // Double reading: player hears "tightened". It's loosened.
    Anin: It's done.
    <<set $gap2_pole_done to true>>
    <<quest_update "gap2" "Go back to bed">>
    // Same as Gap 1: back to the Dorm, where Gap2_Dorm_End is the start
    // node while $gap2_pole_done is true.
    <<scene_transition "Dorm">>
<<else>>
    Anin: It's done.
<<endif>>
===


// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// DORM — 00:00 (END)
// Trigger: Gap2_FlagpoleBase loads the Dorm; this is its start node while
// $gap2_pole_done is true.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------

title: Gap2_Dorm_End
tags: scene4 gap2 dorm
---
// Anin lies down. The clock still reads 00:00.
// Double reading: true, and the worst thing she's said yet.
Anin: He'll be safe from the roof. That's what matters.
// The second hand moves.
<<gap_mode false>>
<<set $chapter_scene to 5>>
<<end_gap>>
// TRANSITION → Scene 5: Day 3. Keep "rooftop_key" in the inventory.
===
